<title>USA: DBA Systems to buy back up to 200,000 shrs.</title>
<headline>DBA Systems to buy back up to 200,000 shrs.</headline>
<dateline>MELBOURNE, Fla. 1997-02-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>DBA Systems Inc said Wednesday it plans to buy back up to 200,000 shares of its common stock.</p>
<p>The transactions are to be made in the open market or in negotiated transactions through August 31, it said.</p>
<p>&quot;This action has been taken based on the board's opinion that, at current market prices, DBA's common shares are undervalued,&quot; Chairman, President and Chief Executive John Slack said in a statement.</p>
<p>DBA's stock was trading Wednesday at about 5-1/8. Its low for the year is 4-3/8 and its high for the year is 6-3/4.</p>
</text>
